# What each profile's own SUnit suites score, as of the last time somebody
# looked.  Read by tests/run_profiles.sh, which `make test` runs.
#
# This is a RATCHET, not a target.  The rule is that neither number may fall:
# a suite that ran 633 tests must still run 633, and a suite that passed 633
# must still pass 633.  Both directions matter, and the first one matters
# more than it looks -- a package whose tests stop being FOUND reports a
# perfect score, and that is exactly the shape of the failure this file
# exists to catch.  The Chronology suites spent a while reporting nothing at
# all because four classes deadlocked the runner, and nothing noticed.
#
# Improving a number fails too, with a message saying so.  That is
# deliberate: an unrecorded improvement is an improvement nothing is
# protecting, and the next regression silently spends it.  Edit the line in
# the same commit that earns it.
#
# Two of these are not at 100%, and are recorded honestly rather than
# excluded:
#
#   pharo-announcements  43/43 -- WeakAnnouncerTest is excluded: it tests
#                                 WEAK announcements, and weak references are
#                                 Phase F work the object memory has not
#                                 done.  The profile says so.
#   pharo-weak           12/32 -- weak references and finalization, which
#                                 the object memory does not implement yet;
#                                 this is Phase F work.
#
# pharo-collections runs Pharo's Set, Dictionary, IdentityDictionary, Bag and
# MethodDictionary against the package's OWN tests, 469 of them, and 410 pass.
# It was 288 until abstract test classes stopped being run: CollectionRootTest
# defines the tests every collection must pass and leaves `collection' a
# subclassResponsibility, so running the parent itself asked a question nobody
# was meant to answer -- 52 errors, each a test doing exactly what it was
# written to do.
# The substitution itself is sound -- the st2026 suites pass on this image
# unchanged -- and what the remaining 182 measure is Collection and Stream
# protocol Pharo assumes and 1983 has no name for, the same grind that took
# Chronology from 275 to 633.
#
# A profile with no SUnit at all (bluebook) is not listed: it has no
# TestCase, so there is nothing to ask it.
#
# profile               run  passed
st2026                  12   12
pharo-announcements     43   43
pharo-time              633  633
pharo-weak              32   12
pharo-collections       469  410
